# Committed reproduction artifacts are generated with LF (every writer in this repo
# passes newline="\n") and are byte-compared by the phase 8 reproduction gate.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, so without these rules a fresh clone would
# check the artifacts out with CRLF, `repro` would regenerate them with LF, and the
# gate would report a reproduction failure that is purely a line-ending artefact --
# on the one command whose entire job is to prove the numbers reproduce.

*.jsonl              text eol=lf
data/cassettes/*.json text eol=lf
data/results/**/*.json text eol=lf
